    "selected_new_checks": [
      "R126: for each fixed positive tube radius, Hausdorff convergence of compact traces gives uniform distance-function convergence; positive distance level sets have zero planar measure, so tubular measures vary continuously. The same-configuration coupling and Markov over the original environment yield R1. Bounded continuous discrepancies give the converse and avoid a separate two-replica law assumption.",
